---
import Base from "../../layouts/Base.astro";

const description = "Use OopBuy warehouse QC photos to check seams, cuffs, hems and loose threads. Compare the photos with the exact seller option before choosing what to do next.";
---
<Base title="OopBuy QC Stitching Check | Review Seams in Warehouse Photos" description={description}>
  <main class="wrap page">
    <p><a class="more" href="/guide/">← OopBuy buying guide</a></p>
    <h1>How to check stitching in OopBuy QC photos</h1>
    <p class="pageintro">Use your warehouse photos to compare the seams on the item you received with the exact color and size from your seller listing.</p>
    <section class="research-panel">
      <h2>What to look for</h2>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Match the item first.</strong> Compare the seller link, selected option and any visible size label. Two variants may have different seams or trim.</li>
        <li><strong>Check the joins and edges.</strong> Look at the collar, cuffs, hems, pocket corners and zipper tape. Look for a gap, broken stitches or a seam pulling away from the fabric.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare both sides.</strong> For paired features such as cuffs and pockets, check their placement and alignment. Ask for a straight-on close-up when an angle or shadow makes the difference hard to see.</li>
      </ol>
    </section>
    <section class="research-panel">
      <h2>When the photo is unclear</h2>
      <p>Point to the exact spot when asking OopBuy about an extra photo, for example, “Could you photograph the inside stitching on the left cuff in good light?” If you see a clearly open seam, keep a photo and check the options available for that order before arranging international shipping.</p>
      <p>A photo can show visible gaps, loose threads and uneven alignment. It cannot confirm how strong a seam is or how it will hold up in use.</p>
      <p><a class="more" href="/finds/">Browse OopBuy finds →</a></p>
    </section>
  </main>
</Base>
<style>
  li {
    margin-block: 0.65rem;
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
</style>
